{
  "_comment": "Retro-grid taps for lnx-server (1920x1080). Copy to touch.json on the host and edit: confirm device with `python3 touch.py --list-devices`, raw range with evtest. Rects are the default 4x3 retro_grid layout; recompute for another W/H with: python3 renderers/retro_grid.py --width <W> --height <H> (paste the output under \"regions\"). Each cell fires the existing allowlisted notify action (transient CELL notice, auto-return); in-grid flash comes from confidence_feedback pointed at renderer retro_grid / input tap -- touch.py POSTs every resolved tap there best-effort AFTER the cell action dispatches. No new generic action; see TOUCH.md (Retro grid wiring).",
  "device": "/dev/input/event8",
  "endpoint": "http://127.0.0.1:8980",
  "width": 1920,
  "height": 1080,
  "calibration": {
    "x_min": 0,
    "x_max": 1920,
    "y_min": 0,
    "y_max": 1080,
    "swap_xy": false,
    "invert_x": false,
    "invert_y": false,
    "rotation": 0
  },
  "tap_max_seconds": 0.5,
  "tap_max_pixels": 40,
  "debounce_seconds": 0.3,
  "confidence_feedback": {
    "enabled": true,
    "renderer": "retro_grid",
    "input": "tap"
  },
